    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey so im working on a schema and its currently in 2nf but its getting kinda messy with redundant data. can u walk me through how to get it to 3nf? specifically what im looking for is how to handle the transitive dependencies so i dont have to update stuff in multiple places",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To achieve 3NF, you need to identify and eliminate transitive dependencies. A transitive dependency occurs when a non-key attribute (higher-order) depends on another non-key attribute (lower-order) that also depends on the primary key. In your schema, you need to ask yourself if a non-key attribute A can be moved to its own table, or if it has a partial dependency on another non-key attribute. If it has a partial dependency, create a new table that includes only the transitive dependent attribute (A). Then, update the original tables to only include the non-key attributes that directly depend on the primary key.",
      "source": "target",
